Expose `setargv.obj` with the MSVC runtime libraries.

GraalVM native-image links `setargv.obj` into a Windows executable for wildcard expansion of the arguments.
It ships next to the other runtime libraries of the MSVC toolset, but the runtime allowlists leave it out, so
lld-link fails with "could not open 'setargv.obj'". Add it to both the dynamic and the static list.
--- a/runtimes/msvc/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/runtimes/msvc/BUILD.bazel
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
     "msvcprt.lib",
     "msvcrt.lib",
     "oldnames.lib",
+    "setargv.obj",
     "vcruntime.lib",
 ]
 
@@ -20,6 +21,7 @@
     "libcpmt.lib",
     "libvcruntime.lib",
     "oldnames.lib",
+    "setargv.obj",
 ]
 
 # Keep LLVM's COM compiler-support dependency separate from the Microsoft STL.
